WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.610
Eighteen mines.

2
00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:04.470
Nearly 2,000 kilometres of railway.

3
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.170
Four port terminals.

4
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.770
One company's system in the Pilbara.

5
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:13.430
Driverless trains carry over 1 million
tonnes of ore a day to the coast.

6
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.630
There it is loaded onto ships.

7
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.670
Most of it is turned into steel abroad.

8
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.390
Mine, railway, port, ship, steelworks.

9
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.890
Somewhere along that chain,
the environment pays a price.

10
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.870
So where along that journey
does the damage happen?

11
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.750
In this mission, you'll follow
the ore from pit to port,

12
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.090
and weigh the evidence on the scheme.

13
00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:36.510
Then you'll judge how
sustainable the trade is,

14
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:39.410
from extraction to the steel it becomes.

15
00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:43.960
Your mission: decide where along iron
ore's journey the damage happens.
